  "mechanism_rationale": "Even with discrete particle priors (Theory 1) and smooth 1-Lipschitz Born-Infeld critics (Theory 2), existing GAN and scalar-horizon OT trainers conflate macroscopic mode mass pi_m (subject to O(1/sqrt(B pi_m)) Poisson batch shot noise) with microscopic local spread sigma_m and conditional base drift A_t(c_i - c_k), while finite screening horizons rho*ell starve gradient transport across missing equidistant modes (img_bars4) and abrupt shifts (target_shift_recovery). RGDT deconflicts scale, mass, and drift via symmetric conformal target metrics, orphan-gated Monge deficit-surplus coupling, exchangeability-invariant pooled-tangent conditional residualization, and MoG kernel-variance-aware prior geometry on fast BF16/Newton-Schulz DualNorm.",
